   Here's a quick tutorial.
   First, to connect to a mud type:

   #ses sessname hostname port

   replacing hostname with the ip address or host name, and
   port with the port number of the mud you want to
   connect to.
   When you're done, quit out of the mud, then type #quit
   to get out of lyntin.  That's all you _need_ to know.

   See also: alias, action, gag, session, help
